    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** serving as the clear cornerstone of the lineup. His elite 79.55 score is buoyed by a favorable matchup against Kolek and a notable wind-out advantage that inflates his raw projection by 5%. Alongside him, **Lars Nootbaar** projects as our strongest outfield play (67.77) due to a highly favorable pairing against Waldrep, whose 7.82 xERA represents the softest landing spot for any of our bats today. **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** also anchor our offensive floor, both benefiting from high-leverage lineup positions at the top of the order, which mitigates the moderate difficulty of the matchup against Jones.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Dillon Dingler** on the pine. Despite a strong underlying xwOBA of 0.386, his score of 36.28 fell below our strict 40.0 floor, primarily due to the severe penalty incurred by facing Eovaldi and the aggressive defensive suppression from an elite hold pitcher. Consequently, we are proceeding with **Luke Raley** and **Christian Yelich** in the outfield; while both face challenges, they maintain higher efficiency scores than **Dillon Dingler** thanks to favorable platoon splits that provide a safer route to production. Managers should keep a close watch on **Chase Meidroth** and **Jacob Gonzalez**, as their sub-50 scores leave them vulnerable to in-game adjustments if the bottom of the order fails to produce early. We remain cautious with **Colt Keith**, whose value is currently throttled by Eovaldi\u2019s ability to limit base-stealing opportunities\u2014a critical metric for our scarcity-driven strategy.",
